Z||000011||stsmithgt||02-28-2000||10:33 AM||||I just thought.(have to mark that on the calander.)  Why stick with counter top?  There are some floor tile companys that have some sweet looking tile made out of just about anything you can think of.  It would be a little more expensive, but it would open up to more of an assortment to choose from.  Talk about choices of color or texture or even material!  I'm sure the edges would clean up better on some more than others.  OUCH! I have to stop thinking now. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000012||william_thorniii||02-28-2000||11:54 AM||||87EC05,<P>Asthetically your suggestion makes sense.  Unfortunately it would not make sense for those with the rallye gage package.  Not to mention that each and every warped console does not warp in the same manner.  Please drop me a line about when you have time this week.  I would like to get your opinion on something.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>937-259-5295||||reg||10
Z||000013||fotofrank||02-28-2000||01:28 PM||||I used a wood laminate for my dash. It looks ok to me but the next one I make I'll be more carefull.  If the black laminate you have is thin enough an exacto  can cut it. I used the trim pannels from my das as a pattern, holding the laminate with large spring clips. This held every thing solid as I cut out the circles and squares for my dash. I posted a picture of my das a few days ago.||||reg||3
